---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Split from '../components/Split.astro';
import Hd from '../components/Hd.astro';
import ProcessDiagram from '../components/ProcessDiagram.astro';
import FindingsDiagram from '../components/FindingsDiagram.astro';
import ScopeTree from '../components/ScopeTree.astro';

// DRAFT. Hidden from search engines (noindex).
// The project was under NDA: the client is anonymised ("Nordic insurer"), but check the client's publishing permission before this goes public.
//  - No company-specific ratings, no client self-assessment and no market leaders' names, in the text or in images.
const scope = [
  { label: 'Markets', leaves: ['Finland', 'Sweden', 'Norway', 'Denmark'] },
  { label: 'Focus', leaves: ['Consumers', 'Car insurance'] },
  { label: 'Channels', leaves: ['Mobile app', 'Web service'] },
  { label: 'Journey', leaves: ['Buying', 'Managing', 'Claims'] },
];
---
<Layout title="Benchmark study – Nordic insurer – Portfolio 2026" description="A competitor benchmark of ten insurers across four Nordic markets, giving the leadership of a Nordic insurer a shared fact base for digital development." current="works" next={{ href: "sok.html", label: "SOK" }} noindex>
<div class="snap">
<Hero image="nordic-hero" alt="Cover collage in Nordic landscapes and everyday scenes: a couple with mugs at the back of a car by a lake, a car on a forest road, a cup on a rainy windowsill and a view in a car mirror, with the word NORDIC in large white letters" heading="Benchmark study – Nordic insurer" />

<Split narrow snug>
<Fragment slot="visual"><ScopeTree label="Scope of the benchmark: markets Finland, Sweden, Norway and Denmark; focus on consumers and car insurance; channels mobile app and web service; journey phases buying, managing and claims. All parts lead to the conclusions." root="Benchmark" end="Conclusions" branches={scope} /></Fragment>
<Fragment slot="title">Nordic benchmark</Fragment>
<Fragment slot="lead">An impartial view of where the insurer’s digital services stand in Nordic competition.</Fragment>
<p>The company is the largest non-life insurer in the Nordics, but its picture of its competitive position was built largely from the inside. In October–December 2024 our team, together with the client’s core team and an eight-person reference group, compared ten insurers across four markets with one framework.</p>
<div class="col" style="gap:calc(12 * var(--u))">
<p class="strong">The company wanted to know three things:</p>
<ul style="gap:calc(8 * var(--u))">
<li>How mature are its digital services compared with competitors in each country?</li>
<li>What are the real competitive advantages it can communicate?</li>
<li>Where should development be focused?</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p>The difficulty was that competitors’ logged-in customer views are closed. We designed the evaluation framework and the research setup so that the information could be gathered from their own customers in a GDPR-compliant way and with copyright respected.</p>
</Split>

<section class="fold">
<Hd style="max-width:calc(760 * var(--u))">
<Fragment slot="title">Approach</Fragment>
We built an evaluation framework that assessed every company in the same way. It had two parts: the customer’s digital self-service and the back-end capabilities of the digital services.
</Hd>
<div class="berg">
<div class="berg-shape">
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="50,0 75,100 25,100" fill="#FAFAFA" stroke="#0B0B14" stroke-width="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg>
</div>
<div class="berg-text">
<div class="col">
<h3>Customer self-service</h3>
<p class="strong">What the customer can do on their own in the app and online.</p>
</div>
<div class="col">
<ul>
<li>Using the service</li>
<li>Communication</li>
<li>Personalisation and cross-sell</li>
<li>Managing billing</li>
<li>Editing policies and profile</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<div class="berg-water"></div>
<div class="berg-shape berg-sub">
<div class="hatch"></div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><polygon points="25,0 75,0 95,100 5,100" fill="none" stroke="#0B0B14" stroke-width="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg>
</div>
<div class="berg-text">
<div class="col">
<h3>Back-end capabilities</h3>
<p class="strong">What sits behind the digital services but is not directly visible to the customer.</p>
</div>
<div class="col">
<ul>
<li>Personalisation</li>
<li>Channel strategy: native, cross-platform or wrapper</li>
<li>Customer-facing AI</li>
<li>APIs and developer portals</li>
<li>Logged-out purchase journey</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="fold">
<div class="hd" style="max-width:calc(900 * var(--u))">
<h2 class="h">Five steps</h2>
<p class="sans lead">The comparison covered 10 competitors in Finland, Sweden, Norway and Denmark. The work proceeded in five steps.</p>
<div class="serif copy" style="max-width:calc(640 * var(--u))">
<p>Our core team did the surveys and interviews, the desk study, the mystery shopping and the analysis of competitors’ digital channels, apps and technology choices ourselves.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="rowpad" style="padding-top:calc(36 * var(--u))">
<div class="tagline"><span class="tag">Oct–Dec 2024</span><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="flow">
<div class="fb s1"><span class="fn">Step 1</span><b>Kick-off and scoping</b><p>The company’s internal interviews and documentation; the scope was validated with the core team and the reference group.</p></div>
<div class="arw a12"><svg class="ar" viewBox="0 0 40 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6H38 M32 1L38 6L32 11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></div>
<div class="fb s2"><span class="fn">Step 2</span><b>Desk study</b><p>Competitors’ public information: apps, developer portals and AI solutions.</p></div>
<div class="arw a23"><svg class="ar" viewBox="0 0 40 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6H38 M32 1L38 6L32 11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></div>
<div class="fb s3"><span class="fn">Step 3</span><b>Customer research</b><p>11 customers of competitors who had car insurance and a claim in the last 12 months. Each answered a survey, and the answers were verified in a one-to-one interview.</p></div>
<div class="wrap"><span class="wv"></span></div>
<div class="fb s4"><span class="fn">Step 4</span><b>Mystery shopping</b><p>The steps of the logged-out purchase journey were documented for every company.</p></div>
<div class="arw a45"><svg class="ar" viewBox="0 0 40 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6H38 M32 1L38 6L32 11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></div>
<div class="fb s5"><span class="fn">Step 5</span><b>Analysis</b><p>Company and country maturity assessments (low–medium–high), the company’s own assessment on the same framework and the Nordic synthesis.</p></div>
<div class="arw a5e"><svg class="ar" viewBox="0 0 40 12" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6H38 M32 1L38 6L32 11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg></div>
<div class="fb se"><span class="fn">Result</span><b>Conclusions</b></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="fold">
<Hd style="max-width:calc(900 * var(--u))">
<Fragment slot="title">From data to decisions</Fragment>
Three data sources, one framework. An LLM assisted with the analysis, with unpacking findings and with phrasing summaries, and a human validated every result: assessments were checked against survey answers, interviews and the desk study before the Nordic synthesis.
</Hd>
<div class="pd">
<ProcessDiagram label="Process diagram: desk study, customer research and mystery shopping feed a shared evaluation framework, which produces strengths, market gaps and a development direction. Assessments are validated against the data." note="Validation: assessments were checked against the data" />
</div>
</section>

<section class="fold">
<Hd style="max-width:calc(900 * var(--u))">
<Fragment slot="title">Findings</Fragment>
Competitors were compared with one framework across four markets. The industry-level findings that can be published sit at the maturity levels like this.
</Hd>
<div class="fd">
<div class="fd-vis">
<FindingsDiagram label="Maturity map: customer self-service on the horizontal axis and back-end capabilities on the vertical axis. Using the service and communication are at the high level, claims and mobile strategies at the medium level, and personalisation and AI at the low level. Finland is at the high level, Sweden, Norway and Denmark at the medium level." />
</div>
<div class="fd-text">
<div class="col">
<div class="tagline"><span class="tag">High level</span><span class="line"></span></div>
<ul>
<li><b>Finland stood out.</b> The Finnish market was the most digitally mature; Sweden, Norway and Denmark settled at the medium level.</li>
<li><b>Using the service and communication work.</b> Customers can use and communicate digitally well.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="col">
<div class="tagline"><span class="tag">Medium level</span><span class="line"></span></div>
<ul>
<li><b>Self-service is everyone’s direction, but claims are still handled by phone.</b> Interviewed customers preferred calling customer service to reporting damage digitally.</li>
<li><b>Mobile strategies vary.</b> Native apps, cross-platform solutions and wrapper apps live side by side, even in different countries of the same company.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="col">
<div class="tagline"><span class="tag">Low level</span><span class="line"></span></div>
<ul>
<li><b>AI showed up in talk, not in customers’ everyday lives.</b> Only one of the compared companies publicly offered generative AI in customer service.</li>
<li><b>Personalisation and cross-sell were the weak spot of the whole industry.</b> Tailored offers are missing from almost everyone.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="fold">
<Hd style="max-width:calc(900 * var(--u))">
<Fragment slot="title">Results and impact</Fragment>
The team wrote the 109-page final report and presented the results to the company’s stakeholders. The report gave the company a shared fact base on its competitive position in each of the four markets and showed the strengths and market-specific gaps where development can be focused. The outside view confirmed the company’s own reading of the market.
</Hd>
<div class="rowpad">
<div class="stats3">
<div class="stat"><div class="big">109</div><div class="lab">Pages in the benchmark report</div></div>
<div class="stat"><div class="big">10</div><div class="lab">Competitors</div></div>
<div class="stat"><div class="big">4</div><div class="lab">Markets</div></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="rowpad">
<div class="impact">
<span class="cap">Impact</span>
<p>The results guided how next year’s development budgets were allocated.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<Footer />
</div>
</Layout>
